{
  "contractVersion": 1,
  "kind": "test-vectors",
  "subject": "public-url",
  "notes": [
    "Whether a URL names a host on the public internet. `setup` asks it of the community URL and writes the answer as DHT_REACHABILITY: public, or private for everything else, and the dht node starts accordingly.",
    "The host is judged as it was written, not as a WHATWG parser would rewrite it: that parser turns `http://2130706433` into 127.0.0.1 and a C reader does not, so both implementations take the host out of the text by the same rule and read an address the way inet_pton does -- four decimal parts without leading zeros, or RFC 4291 text. Anything else numeric is private.",
    "A name is public unless it has no dot or ends in a label reserved for a network that is not the internet. Whether it resolves is not asked: `setup` runs where DNS may not yet point at the machine, and the operator called it the public URL."
  ],
  "fields": {
    "id": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "Stable forever. A failure names this."
    },
    "why": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "What this vector is load bearing for."
    },
    "url": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "The URL as the community row holds it."
    },
    "expect.public": {
      "type": "bool",
      "note": "The contract."
    }
  },
  "count": 41,
